Subject: let the guest have its own host name with --hostname

RabbitMQ failed to boot in ThothDock with "epmd error for host
DESKTOP-...: address": Erlang names its node after uname(2)'s node name,
which under PRoot is the device's (or desktop's) own, while the container's
/etc/hosts names the container. Docker gives each container its own UTS
namespace, so hostname, gethostname() and uname -n report the container's
host name there.

--hostname=NAME makes uname report NAME as the node name. Only uname is
intercepted, at its exit, and only the nodename field is rewritten; the
release, machine and hwcap stay the kernel's, sethostname is left alone.
PRoot's kompat extension (--kernel-release) rewrites the whole utsname, and
extensions run newest first, so --hostname must come before
--kernel-release on the command line (ThothDock passes them in that order).
kompat itself was not used for this: it adds ptrace stops on epoll_pwait,
accept4, dup3 and eventfd2, which every event-loop server would pay for.

Upstream: termux/proot @ 7266fb3e8516535682f5a9c8f3a7e70f6506eddb (v5.1.107.92), after patches 0001-0012

